 "_doc": "The ONE place the ONNX Runtime version is pinned (issue #85). libarc's CMake build (cmake/vendor_onnxruntime.cmake) fetches the archive for the target platform, checks the archive's sha256 and the library's sha256, and copies the library + its licence next to libarc (<build>/onnxruntime/), with onnxruntime.json; the model server loads that copy (model_server/app/nft2.py) and checks its sha256 again at load. Each platform lists ordered \"sources\" (tried in turn: a cached archive first, then each url): every archive is checked against its own sha256, and the library extracted from it against the platform's ONE lib_sha256, so a mirror can only ever yield the exact pinned bytes. github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime went offline in Nov 2026 (release downloads 404), hence the extra sources (NuGet: Microsoft's own package; our Dropbox mirror of the original archive, where listed). A source may set \"licence\" when its licence files sit elsewhere. An archive already in ARC_ORT_CACHE under its url's file name is used without downloading; the top-level url/sha256/root/lib are the original GitHub source (sources[0]), kept for reference. linux-x64/linux-arm64 list only GitHub (no Linux installer ships; add a mirror when one does). model_server/pyproject.toml pins the Python wheel (the embedder, Steer TTS) to the same version (from PyPI); model_server/tests/test_bindings.py fails when the two differ. To move to another version: update version + every platform entry and its sources (archive sha256, lib_sha256 of the extracted library), pyproject.toml's onnxruntime==, uv lock, rebuild, run the ear tests.",
